If the parser only accepts a file path:

```c
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stddef.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <fcntl.h>

extern int parse_image_file(const char *path);

int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *data, size_t size) {
    char path[] = "/tmp/fuzzimgXXXXXX";
    int fd = mkstemp(path);
    if (fd < 0) return 0;
    if (write(fd, data, size) != (ssize_t)size) { close(fd); unlink(path); return 0; }
    close(fd);
    parse_image_file(path);
    unlink(path);
    return 0;
}
```

Build and run:

```sh
clang -g -O1 -fsanitize=fuzzer,address,undefined fuzz_parser.c image_parser.c -o fuzz_parser
mkdir corpus && cp samples/*.png corpus/   # optional seed corpus
./fuzz_parser corpus -max_len=1048576
```

Key points: the harness must be deterministic, free of leaks in the harness itself, and the target must handle any byte sequence without crashing — ASan/UBSan will turn bugs into fuzzer findings.
